ory ran empty on a night when its only candidates were Economist analysis pieces. 72-hour window because these publish a few items a day."}],"coverage":{"search":"unconstrained","prefer":["complete","authoritative","accessible"],"mark_subscriber_links":true,"discovery_per_category":false,"discovery_note":"Retired 2026-10-18 in favour of signal feeds and the per-source tally on the cuts page."},"editorial":{"two_axes":true,"summary_length":"2 to 4 sentences","summary_rule":"original prose, written from coverage the agent read; no verbatim passages beyond a short attributed quote","mark_thin_summaries":true},"evolution":{"mode":"propose"},"category_scope_notes":{"finance-and-economics":"Give room to the financing of the AI build-out: debt loads at AI infrastructure companies, bond and credit-default-swap moves, hyperscaler capital spending, and the market''s exposure to it. Owner''s standing interest, 2026-10-17.","business":"Same emphasis as Finance and economics on the AI build-out and its risks, from the company side: capex, contracts, concentration, and who bears the losses if demand slows."},"source_roles":{"agenda":"Sets what is significant today. The editor ranks from these desks'' judgment. Three desks: the New York Times, the Economist, the Wall Street Journal.","signal":"Corroborates and widens the aperture. Items are candidates like any other, judged on consequence; a story only these feeds surfaced is the measure of what the agenda missed. Added 2026-10-17 to replace web-search discovery, after AP, Reuters and the BBC proved unreachable to the search tool. AP and Reuters publish no usable feed."}}', 'seed'
